        "title": "fix(dispatch-wrapper): fix flock separator and script command detection",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n1. **flock `--`**: `flock /tmp/lock -- echo hello` not unwrapped (-- treated as option-like token)\n2. **script command detection**: `script -- echo hello` mislabeled echo as transcript file\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- flock: skip past `--` separator\n- script: detect `--` separator form vs transcript-file form; transcript-only stays blocked\n\n## User Impact\n\nFixes command execution analysis for flock/script with `--` separator.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Runtime proof — flock/script unwrap verified (Node 24):**\n\n![proof](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/proof-screenshots/pr-98657-proof-v2.png)\n\n- `exec-wrapper-resolution.test.ts`: 132/132 passed ✅\n- `exec-approvals-allow-always.test.ts`: 48/48 passed ✅",
